Pre-release review 2026-09-29.

Kubernetes::Comb::Client::Async needs ensure, update_status and patch_status of Net::Async::Kubernetes. Those arrive with 0.009; the version on CPAN is 0.008 and has none of them (checked against the 0.008 tag). The module loads Net::Async::Kubernetes with require_module and no version, so with 0.008 installed it loads fine and every deploy and status write then fails with "Can't locate object method ..." inside a Future -- reconcile reports phase Error with that text.

SPEC section 4: Client::Async "loads them at runtime and dies with a clear message naming the missing module". A too-old module is the same situation.

Wanted:
- Loading Kubernetes::Comb::Client::Async with Net::Async::Kubernetes < 0.009 dies like the missing-module case, naming the module, the version needed and the version found.
- t/client-async.t and the async part of t/examples.t skip instead of fail when the installed version is too old; t/client-async-missing.t keeps its claim.
- A regression test for the too-old case that needs no particular installed version.
- The unit suite stays green with the released 0.008 on the include path and with 0.009.

Verified before filing: prove -lr t/ is green against the sources of the released tags (IO::K8s 1.108, Kubernetes::REST 1.108, Net::Async::Kubernetes 0.008) -- t/client-async.t passes there because it never calls the missing methods.

